  "_reconciled_2026_09_13": "MCO1b — this file and contracts/nexus-interaction-contract.js's SYSTEMS.guardian block had drifted from each other and from guardian/server.js's real routes. Reconciled against server.js directly (grep for every real pathname===/startsWith check), not against either prior file. Findings: (1) both files were partially right, partially stale — neither was the correct source alone. (2) real routes present in server.js but missing from BOTH prior files, now added below: /forge/health, /open/*, /providers/*/spawn, /queue/compartments/*, /cli/exec, /api/guardian/cfr/state, /api/guardian/hooks/summary, /api/guardian/nerve/snapshot, /api/guardian/cfr/event, /api/guardian/organism-queue(+/:id/zip,+/:id/ack), /build, /api/intake(+/verdict,+/promote,+/rollback), /api/copilot/prompt, /chatgpt-mode/query, /command/tools, /wake-job-ack, /guardian-ui/*, /ui/*, /api/account-identity, /channel, /result, /heartbeat, /baseline, /stream/*, /seam/queues/*, /seam/sessions/*, /lab*. (3) a REAL LIVE BUG found, not just doc drift: /memory/ledger, /memory/artifacts, /memory/stats, and bare /ledger were listed here as real routes and are called by real client code (guardian/server.js's own embedded dashboard JS at loadDB()/updateSB(), and guardian/guardian-api.js's memoryStats()/memoryIngest()) — but grepped server.js directly for a handler and none exists. These calls 404 today. Removed from this file's routes (they are not real), left here as a named, open bug for whoever picks it up — implementing the missing handler is out of MCO1's scope (doc-reconciliation only), not silently patched here. (4) contracts/nexus-interaction-contract.js's SYSTEMS.guardian.jobs claimed a per-job route at /jobs/:jobId — wrong; the real per-job routes are /status/:jobId and /response/:jobId, and bare /jobs is a list endpoint, confirmed separately. That central file still needs its own per-system split into MCO3/Track B — this fixes guardian's own copy only.",
